  "id": "COMPOUND:17163 - PROTEIN:6151",
  "verbalization": "Norarecoline is implicated in the biological pathway leading to Ataxin-2 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Norarecoline targets Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is subsequently targeted by multiple compounds, including 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol and (1R,2S,6R,7R,10S,11R,12R,14S)-10,11-dihydroxy-2,6-dimethyl-12-propan-2-yl-13-oxatetracyclo[8.5.0.02,7.012,14]pentadecane-6-carboxylic acid. All these compounds share a common target, Ataxin-2, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving the SDR family of enzymes. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Norarecoline in modulating the activity of SDR family members, which in turn may influence Ataxin-2 through direct or indirect interactions. The evidence supports a link between Norarecoline and Ataxin-2 via a chain of targets, emphasizing the importance of SDR family members in this biological relationship.",
